From: challoc <noreply@chainguard.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] memefficiency: start defrag before the replicaof flush
 under challoc

"Active defrag can't be triggered during replicaof database flush. See
issue #14267" needs active defrag to be running when the sync's flush
runs, which is within a few ms of REPLICAOF, before the next cron tick.
The bundled jemalloc still holds about 22 MB of fragmentation when the
flush ends, so defrag starts on what the flush leaves. challoc gives the
freed memory back as the flush frees it (slab pages close the freed pages
and empty slabs leave the bins, chainguard-project-theseus/challoc#604), so defrag would
start only if a defrag decision fell between the deletes and the flush,
and the test fails with "defrag not started.". Under MALLOC=challoc the
replica now waits for defrag to start on the fragmentation the test's
deletes leave, at the stock active-defrag-ignore-bytes, before it sends
REPLICAOF: defrag runs during the flush, which is what the test is for.

The change goes through a helper, challoc_or, which returns the challoc
value when mem_allocator contains "challoc" and the stock value
otherwise, so the bundled-jemalloc build runs the file unchanged.

No other test in the file needs a calibration: with slab pages, challoc
meets every stock fragmentation target (the "eval scripts", "IDMP
streams", "HFE", "argv retained", "big list" and "template-encoded
hashes" tests, which challoc's slab floor used to fail).
---
 tests/unit/memefficiency.tcl | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/unit/memefficiency.tcl b/tests/unit/memefficiency.tcl
--- a/tests/unit/memefficiency.tcl
+++ b/tests/unit/memefficiency.tcl
@@ -85,6 +85,17 @@ test "Active defrag handles equal fragmentation thresholds" {
 } {} {defrag external:skip tsan:skip standalone}
 
 run_solo {defrag} {
+    # challoc_or CHALLOC_VALUE VALUE: CHALLOC_VALUE under MALLOC=challoc
+    # (mem_allocator contains "challoc"), VALUE otherwise, for a step a
+    # test takes from the bundled jemalloc's behaviour where challoc's
+    # differs. The bundled-jemalloc build runs the file unchanged.
+    proc challoc_or {challoc_value value} {
+        if {[string match {*challoc*} [s mem_allocator]]} {
+            return $challoc_value
+        }
+        return $value
+    }
+
     proc wait_for_defrag_stop {maxtries delay {expect_frag 0}} {
         wait_for_condition $maxtries $delay {
             [s active_defrag_running] eq 0 && ($expect_frag == 0 || [s allocator_frag_ratio] <= $expect_frag)
@@ -1454,6 +1465,23 @@ run_solo {defrag} {
 
                 catch {$replica config set activedefrag yes} e
                 if {[$replica config get activedefrag] eq "activedefrag yes"} {
+                    # challoc: defrag has to be running when the sync's flush
+                    # runs, which is within a few ms of REPLICAOF, before the
+                    # next cron tick. The bundled jemalloc still holds about
+                    # 22 MB of fragmentation then, so defrag starts on what the
+                    # flush leaves; challoc gives the freed memory back as the
+                    # flush frees it, so it would start only if a defrag
+                    # decision fell between the deletes and the flush. Under
+                    # challoc, wait for defrag to start on what the deletes
+                    # left before REPLICAOF, so that it runs during the flush.
+                    if {[challoc_or 1 0]} {
+                        wait_for_condition 50 100 {
+                            [s total_active_defrag_time] ne 0
+                        } else {
+                            puts [$replica info memory]
+                            fail "defrag not started before replicaof."
+                        }
+                    }
                     # Start replication sync which will flush the replica's database,
                     # then enable defrag to run concurrently with the database flush.
                     $replica replicaof $master_host $master_port
